WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.400
While the Galactic Empire expanded its power

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.150
and began absorbing neighboring star systems,

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.820
some of the outer frontier planets

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.820
maintained independent governments.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.240
The third planet in Tau Ceti system,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.410
Sea of the Morningstar, was a newly settled frontier planet.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.580
As with most newly settled planets,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.130
once generations passed and its population increased,

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.210
relations with its overseer, the Stellar Alliance, worsened,

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.880
and a war of independence began.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.050
To complement their meager fleet,

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.840
the government of Sea of the Morningstar

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.350
issued a new type of edict,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.310
Letter of Marque
the Letter of Marque.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:46.480
Papers in hand, space pirates attacked Stellar Alliance vessels,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.940
greatly contributing to the revolution's success.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.900
This story begins more than one hundred years later,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.950
the war having ended in surprising fashion.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.450
Time for some piracy!

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.720
Wow, that's fast.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.730
Is she all right?

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.600
Yeah,

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.560
at this rate of deceleration, she's fine.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.530
Assuming she leaves orbit right now...

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.490
She'll overshoot it.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.660
Probably land straight in the ocean.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.200
You don't think she's trying to cut it as close as possible?

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.740
She was too quick on the reverse thrusters for that.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.710
The type who tries to cut it perfectly close

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.040
is always late on the thrusters.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.960
What's she thinking?

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.710
Look at you, Mr. Great Pilot.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.130
Can't you even discern a rookie's thoughts?

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.180
What is she doing?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.810
She's maximizing her profile, to increase her rate of deceleration.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.850
That will let her decelerate quickly without burning any propellant.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.110
Aerobraking.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.990
Where'd she learn a rudimentary trick like that?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.170
She's watching atmospheric distribution?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.790
Scary kid...

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.840
It's pretty rude to call her a kid.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.340
After all, she is his daughter.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.840
Her ability to do that doesn't surprise me at all.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.690
Landing location confirmed.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.610
No problems with the pilot or ship.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:22.030
I'll skip the check and briefings...

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:23.950
I'll be leaving early!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.620
Goodbye!

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.780
Good work.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.250
We should get going as well.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.660
Don't you want to know where she's going?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:34.580
Where she's going?

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.310
Wow!

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.350
So cool!

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.600
She probably went home.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:02.610
Over there.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.400
Lamp House

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.540
Welcome!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.210
W-What is this place?

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.370
A café.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.500
It's a bit anachronistic, though.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.760
Anachronistic?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.420
It's just old.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.470
It's not unusual around here.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:32.220
It doesn't use robots or androids, so it's cheap.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.430
Peaceful...

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:39.440
Just a moment.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.070
Welcome.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.820
Have you decided on your order?

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:44.490
Yes.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.280
Cold-brewed coffee...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:48.610
What's today's special?

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:51.830
The South Alicia classic tea.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.910
Can you recommend something else?

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.660
The jasmine tea has grown well this year.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.750
If you aren't from around here, I definitely recommend it.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.630
Then we'll take that.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.760
Cold-brewed coffee and the jasmine tea.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:05.760
Got it!

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:12.100
She learned the daily specials as soon as she got here.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.770
Then I guess she's a good waitress.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.770
Please drink the rest while it's still hot.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.020
Enjoy your drinks.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.480
Kato Marika?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.740
Um, have we met?

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.330
I've never met you before,

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.250
but I'm an old friend of your mother.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.250
You're quite similar.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.090
Oh, I see!

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.710
Thank you.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.760
Have you ever been into space?

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.760
Yes!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.890
Up to the relay station, for my school club.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.430
The yacht club?

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.970
You've heard of us?

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:59.810
Our yacht club maintains a private section at the station.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.520
Sometimes I go up there to work on the practice ships.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.150
I see.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.360
That's amazing.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.860
Have you ever considered viewing the planet from farther away?

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.280
Not just from satellite orbit...

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.990
But from outer space?

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:14.530
Outer space?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.620
That'd be nice!

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:44.860
I'm back.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.230
Voice print verified.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.570
Disabling security.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.830
Pot-au-feu.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.080
It'll be ready soon.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.210
Give me a second.

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.330
Okay.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.180
Hey, Ririka?

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.180
Yeah?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:21.520
I met someone at work today who said they knew you.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.850
Knew me?

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:23.940
Who?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:24.600
I dunno.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:29.860
But they asked if I'd ever want to see the planet from outer space.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.610
So maybe they work in space?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.910
I see...

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:41.120
They arrived sooner than I expected.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.040
But it'll be fine.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:48.880
The seas of space...

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.380
...belong to me.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:53.970
I knew it!

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.630
The minute she brought it up, I knew it had to be you.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:56.760
Are they wearing mourning attire?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.560
Of course a legendary woman like you would figure it out.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.890
We don't have to stand around talking.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:03.980
Come sit down.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.190
Thanks, Ririka.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.860
But first, I must tell you something.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.820
The Captain of the Bentenmaru,

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.240
Gonzaemon Kato, has passed away.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.030
Me too?

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.910
You don't have to drink it.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.200
But today is special.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.000
Tonight, at least,

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.620
we must raise a glass to that good-for-nothing.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.380
May Captain Gonzaemon

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.800
find his place among the stars.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.140
It was just two days ago.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.600
I didn't hear of any battles important enough to make news.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.480
So what finally did the old man in,

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.190
after everything else that has happened?

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.570
Food poisoning.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.740
Food poisoning?

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:58.160
He got food poisoning, and that was that.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.160
I told him to stop eating stuff he picked up off the ground.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:01.990
And so?

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:05.110
When did you say they confirmed his death?

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.370
Two days ago, Galactic Standard Time.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.000
No, twenty seconds ago, it became three days.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.460
To our good-for-nothing captain!

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.550
There's plenty of wine left.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.260
Glad to hear it.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.730
Anyway, I'm impressed you were able to find my house.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.810
You thought you could live here unnoticed?

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.980
Yep.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.480
That optimism of yours hasn't changed at all.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.230
I'm sure that

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.400
this wouldn't have been Captain Kato's first choice, either, but...

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.290
And so...

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:50.330
You are Captain Gonzaemon's eldest child, Kato Marika,

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.080
and we are here to see you.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.630
Um, may I say something?

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:57.340
Yes?

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:01.010
You keep talking about this Gonzaemon captain person.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:02.010
Who is that?

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.810
Ririka! You never told her?

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:08.060
I forgot all about it...

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.640
Until just now.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.570
Gonzaemon Kato was my husband.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.980
Your father.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:21.030
How would you like to captain the space pirate ship, the Bentenmaru?

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.310
Only the previous captain's

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.390
direct descendant may captain the ship.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.140
And right now, you are

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.650
Captain Kato's only daughter in the universe.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.810
You're the only one

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.610
who can become captain.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.070
So—

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.570
W-Wait a second!

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.070
My dad was a pirate?

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:02.700
What's a pirate?

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.660
A space pirate.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.780
You've heard of them.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:06.490
But...

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.620
But that's ancient history!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:11.290
They were part of the war of independence or something.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.750
But aren't they gone now?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.790
No one ever said they were gone.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.920
We're real-life pirates.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:20.590
And we're the crew of the space pirate ship, the Bentenmaru.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:21.720
I'm the medic,

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.130
and he's the helmsman.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:25.720
Hi.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.930
U-Uh,

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.930
are you three trying to trick me?

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.730
Is this some kind of prank?

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.060
Ririka, you never explained anything to her?

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:39.360
I was waiting for the right time.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.360
The right time?

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.860
You wanted to go into space, right?

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.110
If you become captain,

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.280
the Bentenmaru will go wherever you wish!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:47.780
No!

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:51.290
I refuse to do something that would make me a criminal!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.000
Don't worry about that.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.080
Letter of Marque

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:58.710
We have an official pirating license, called a Letter of Marque,

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.130
so we're legal pirates.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:01.050
Legal?!

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.720
Actually...

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.430
Who ever heard of a legal pirate?!

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:25.320
Letters of Marque...

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.490
"The captain of the space pirate ship, the Bentenmaru,

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.740
perished in an unfortunate accident.

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:35.460
The Bentenmaru's pirating license is currently in a grace period."

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:36.540
It's true.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.580
There really are legal pirates.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.020
<i>Time for some piracy!</i>

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.020
Ririka!

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:01.360
Take your time, and think it over.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.120
What is it?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.660
Up all night studying?

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.920
Hey, Mami, have you ever heard of space pirates?

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.750
What are those?

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.050
Is this a history question?

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:24.880
Yeah...

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.470
That's what you'd think.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.260
Anyway, did you hear?

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:33.060
The new teacher's a guy!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:35.020
Oh, which class?

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.640
What?

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.560
The replacement teacher for our class.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.770
And he's young!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.560
So they already chose one?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:44.190
That was fast.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.730
Yeah!

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:47.690
Our school's pretty famous.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.660
They were probably extra-strict with their interviews.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.410
But it's only been a week.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.240
And he's supposed to be pretty cute too.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.250
He's so cute!

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:12.340
I'll be taking over for Mr. Kipling, who's in the hospital

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.140
following last week's accident.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.760
Teacher: Kane McDougal
First Year, Snow Class

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.930
My name is Kane McDougal.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.270
Nice to meet you all.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:24.230
Strict interviews, huh?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:28.440
Also, I hate to disappoint everyone,

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.900
but I'm married.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.200
Additionally,

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.410
I have one more announcement.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.250
Kurihara, come in.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.090
Chiaki Kurihara.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.550
Her parents are transferring from the Uzumasa star system,

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:53.340
so she's come here from the Sea of the Foreststar branch of our school.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.100
My name is Chiaki Kurihara.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:59.270
Nice to meet you all.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.070
She's cute...

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:09.900
I'm sure it will be confusing for you,

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:12.610
with both a new teacher and transfer student.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.570
But it's nearly summer vacation.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:16.830
Chiaki, have a seat...

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.580
Attendance
Sheet

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:23.830
over there.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:24.710
Yes.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.340
She's kinda cool...

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.720
And cute, too.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:55.610
Okay, I'll take attendance.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.580
Oh, my...

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.380
I was so nervous!

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.170
I can't imagine who'd want to teach at a girls' high school!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:11.260
Oh,

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.260
I thought it was every guy's dream.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:16.090
I take that back.

00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:19.890
So did you look at the students' data?

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.470
Lots of potential candidates.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:21.770
Talvikki Launo

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.180
A talented gamer.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:23.480
One who was arrested in middle school for an information crime.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.270
Lynn Lambretta

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:26.230
One who was arrested in middle school for an information crime.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.520
What kind of girls' school is this?

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.070
What about this one?

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:33.190
A transfer student, at this time of year?

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.280
Transfer

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:34.610
Chiaki Kurihara

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:35.030
A transfer student, at this time of year?

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:35.240
She's from your class.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.530
Wants to join yacht club.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:40.200
So she wants to join the yacht club, huh?

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.040
Very suspicious.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.660
Almost as suspicious as we are.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.920
We can have the Bentenmaru look into her.

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.710
And Mr. Kane here will look after her.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.130
I'm counting on you.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.130
So, how's the yacht club?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.140
They're off today for a server check.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.180
The young lady is at her part-time job.

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:03.270
Oh, crap!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:04.140
I forgot!

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.520
Lamp
House

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.350
Welcome!

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:13.350
Hey, aren't we getting some unusual customers today?

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.530
We'll sit over there.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:25.870
Yeah, that's her.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.120
Come to think of it, you're right.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:27.500
De

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:27.870
li
Come to think of it, you're right.

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:28.250
cious
